icleshow/133235142.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2001-scientists-tested-4-beluga-whales-at-a-new-york-aquarium-98-sessions-later-it-was-found-the-arctic-whales-may-recognise-themselves/articleshow/133235142.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T15:09:33+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133235380,imgsize-168818.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado’s 2024 restoration efforts for Preble’s mouse gain momentum with new habitat project]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133233617.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Colorado is taking significant steps to ensure the survival of the endangered Preble's meadow jumping mouse. Efforts focus on restoring essential streamside ecosystems and linking them to floodplains. Landowners are invited to join this initiative through voluntary conservation measures and financial support. A conservation bank was established in 2024 to facilitate these vital restoration projects, with new initiatives rolling out in 2026 to enhance habitat safeguarding.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-colorado-stepped-up-restoration-for-the-prebles-meadow-jumping-mouse-two-years-later-a-new-project-is-expanding-habitat-protection/articleshow/133233617.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-colorado-stepped-up-restoration-for-the-prebles-meadow-jumping-mouse-two-years-later-a-new-project-is-expanding-habitat-protection/articleshow/133233617.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T15:09:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133233783,imgsize-84953.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wyoming fossils reveal ancient forests collapsed after extreme global warming]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133233279.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wyoming-fossils-reveal-ancient-forests-collapsed-during-extreme-global-warming-and-took-over-100000-years-to-recover-a-stark-warning-for-todays-climate/articleshow/133233279.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wyoming-fossils-reveal-ancient-forests-collapsed-during-extreme-global-warming-and-took-over-100000-years-to-recover-a-stark-warning-for-todays-climate/articleshow/133233279.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T14:26:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133234040,imgsize-1710314.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Egyptian archaeologists uncover 3 tombs, 5 mummies, and Roman remains]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133231962.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Egyptian archaeological mission has uncovered three tombs at the Sheikh Sobi site. These burials include mummies and sarcophagi from the Late and Roman periods. One tomb contained five mummies, dating to the Late Period. The other two tombs are believed to be from the Roman period. These discoveries offer insights into the Bahariya Oasis's ancient communities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egyptian-archaeologists-discover-3-tombs-in-bahariya-oasis-with-5-mummies-and-roman-era-remains/articleshow/133231962.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egyptian-archaeologists-discover-3-tombs-in-bahariya-oasis-with-5-mummies-and-roman-era-remains/articleshow/133231962.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T13:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133232250,imgsize-224640.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Great Barrier Reef coral cover rebounds to 35.1% despite bleaching]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133230206.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2025-coral-cover-in-the-great-barrier-reefs-northern-region-fell-to-30-after-its-largest-annual-decline-on-record-a-year-later-surveys-of-192-reefs-found-it-had-risen-to-35-1-despite-another-bleaching-event/articleshow/133230206.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2025-coral-cover-in-the-great-barrier-reefs-northern-region-fell-to-30-after-its-largest-annual-decline-on-record-a-year-later-surveys-of-192-reefs-found-it-had-risen-to-35-1-despite-another-bleaching-event/articleshow/133230206.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T13:59:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133230260,imgsize-525669.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Shakespeare's birth home was nearly shipped to US in 1847; it was saved from a showman's fantasy with a payment of £3,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133232772.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In the 1840s, Shakespeare's birthplace in Stratford-upon-Avon faced the threat of sale, as American showman P.T. Barnum aimed to move the historic home to New York. A dedicated committee formed, rallying public donations and support from notable figures like Prince Albert to save the site. Their efforts culminated in the successful acquisition of the house at auction in 1847, ensuring the preservation of this cherished cultural landmark.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/shakespeares-birth-home-was-about-to-be-shipped-to-the-us-in-1847-the-shakespeare-trust-had-to-buy-it-for-3000-to-save-it-from-a-showman-who-wanted-to-make-it-a-theme-park-attraction/articleshow/133232772.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/shakespeares-birth-home-was-about-to-be-shipped-to-the-us-in-1847-the-shakespeare-trust-had-to-buy-it-for-3000-to-save-it-from-a-showman-who-wanted-to-make-it-a-theme-park-attraction/articleshow/133232772.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T13:36:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133232921,imgsize-119823.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Morocco is testing a 'sponge' pavement that stays 16°F cooler by itself, aims at replacing black asphalt]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133230174.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Morocco is pioneering a novel sponge pavement designed to enhance water management and mitigate heat effects. Unlike conventional black asphalt, this innovative surface enables water to seep through, promoting natural cooling through evaporation when moisture exists. This initiative aims to bolster urban climate resilience and elevate the comfort of residents, with pilot projects underway in Marrakech and Agadir as part of a larger sustainable city initiative.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/morocco-is-testing-a-sponge-pavement-to-replace-black-asphalt-on-roads-in-marrakech-and-agadir-can-run-up-to-16f-cooler-by-itself/articleshow/133230174.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://tim